cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Gay.jl in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Gay.jl: Wide-gamut color sampling with splittable determinism"
abstract: >
  Gay.jl is a Julia package for wide-gamut deterministic color sampling with
  Strong Parallelism Invariance (SPI) on a splittable random substrate.
  It includes NextColorBandwidth, a runnable Shannon-tight kernel-abstraction
  benchmark whose unit is bits/s through a perceptual JND filter, with SPI
  fingerprint verification per run.
authors:
